target_verses.display_text:
He spread out His dwelling like a vine and destroyed His festival.
The Lord forgot what He had made in Zion of festival and Sabbath;
in His angry indignation He provoked king, priest and ruler.

verses.display_text:
All her beauty has departed from Daughter Zion.
Her rulers have become like rams finding no pasture;
they went without strength before the pursuer.

target_verses.display_text:
A psalm for Asaph.
God, nations entered Thine inheritance;
they defiled Thy holy temple;
they made Jerusalem into a fruit-watchman’s hut.

verses.display_text:
A watch was kept over my acts of ungodliness;
they were intertwined in my hands and rose upon my neck.
My strength weakened, because the Lord put pains into my hands; I will not be able to stand.

May all their wickedness come before Thee,
and glean them as they made a gleaning for all my sins;
for my groans are many and my heart is grieved.

target_verses.display_text:
Let the groaning of those in bonds enter before Thee;
according to the greatness of Thine arm,
preserve the sons of those put to death.

verses.display_text:
The Lord drowned without sparing all Jacob’s beautiful things.
In His fury He brought down Daughter Judah’s strongholds;
He pressed them to the earth and profaned her king and her rulers.

He drew His bow like an enemy and made His right hand firm like an opponent.
He killed everything desired by my eyes in Daughter Zion’s tent;
He poured out His fury like fire.

The Lord became like an enemy; He drowned Israel.
He drowned all her citadels and destroyed his strongholds;
He multiplied humiliation and abasement for Daughter Judah.

He spread out His dwelling like a vine and destroyed His festival.
The Lord forgot what He had made in Zion of festival and Sabbath;
in His angry indignation He provoked king, priest and ruler.

target_verses.display_text:
We did not see our signs;
there is no prophet any longer,
and he will know us no longer.

verses.display_text:
Your prophets saw futile things and folly for you.
They did not uncover your injustice to turn back your captivity;
they saw for you futile pronouncements and expulsions.

The Lord did what He intended; He fulfilled His words,
which He commanded from ancient days. He brought down without sparing;
He made the enemy rejoice over you and exalted your oppressor’s horn.

target_verses.display_text:
Hope in Him, all the assembly of the people;
pour out your hearts before Him.
God is our helper. Diapsalma.

Thou didst remove my acquaintances far from me;
they made me an abomination to themselves.
I was handed over and did not go out.

While I was at peace, He scattered me;
He took me by the hair and tore me apart,
and set me up like a target.

They surrounded me with spears,
striking my kidneys without sparing;
they poured my gall onto the earth.

I remembered ancient days
and meditated on all Thy works;
I was pondering the works of Thy hands.

Wait for the Lord;
act courageously, and let your heart be strong,
and wait for the Lord.

Our soul was rescued like a little bird
from the trap of hunters;
the trap was shattered, and we were rescued.

Lord, hear my voice;
let Thine ears be attentive
to the voice of my petition.

Lord, hear my voice;
let Thine ears be attentive
to the voice of my petition.

Those seeking my soul used violence;
those seeking evils for me spoke vain things
and meditated on deceptions all day long.

Give them according to their works
and according to the wickedness of their practices;
give them according to the works of their hands;
repay their recompense to them.

You priests, speak to the heart of Jerusalem; comfort her.
For her humiliation is fulfilled, her sin is loosed;
for from the hand of the Lord she has received double for her sins.
